        "name": "The Hook-First Rule",
        "body": "Never write a literal color where an `--slds-g-*` hook exists. A literal hex is permitted only for admin-chosen Custom tones and for hues SLDS has no hook for.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Accent Rule",
        "body": "In chrome, brand blue is the only accent. Hue variety belongs to the tile content an admin configures, not to the editor's own furniture.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One-Token-Source Rule",
        "body": "Studio tokens (`--newton-studio-*`) are defined once, in the CSS-only module `newtonSelectorFlowCpeUtilityTokens`; every studio stylesheet `@import`s it. Change a token there, never redeclare it in a component.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tint-Not-Fill Rule",
        "body": "State surfaces are `color-mix(in oklab)` tints of the tone (3% rest, 6% hover, 12% selected) over the base surface. Full-strength fills are reserved for the Fill selection style and for check badges.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Weight-Not-Size Rule",
        "body": "Differentiate within a tile by weight and ink color before size. Title and subtitle differ by 2px and a weight step.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono-For-Machines Rule",
        "body": "Monospace marks values a machine will read. It is never a decorative eyebrow or label voice.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Padding-Is-The-Dial Rule",
        "body": "Internal tile rhythm derives from one padding value. Do not add per-layout hardcoded gaps.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Fixed-Column Rule",
        "body": "Grid tiles never grow to fill the row. Predictable size beats full-bleed fill.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One-Tile-Family Rule",
        "body": "Studio pickers never size tiles per group. A picker that needs a different shape changes the glyph or shape drawn inside the framed cell, never the tile's size, surface, padding or selection style.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The State-Driven Lift Rule",
        "body": "Tiles move at most 1-2px, and only on hover, and only for Outlined, Raised and Floating. Selection never translates or resizes a tile.",
